   - Inniaz is a **4/4 flyer** that **buffs all attacking flyers** and has a powerful **3+ flyers attack trigger**.\n\
   - With Warden and Tide Skimmer already in play, we now have **three flyers**, which will trigger Inniaz’s ability.\n\
\n\
2. **Tempo**:\n\
   - Playing Inniaz now puts immense pressure on the opponent. They have no flyers to block, so we can swing for **10 damage in the air** next turn (Warden 2 + Tide Skimmer 3 + Inniaz 4 + potential buffs).\n\
   - The opponent’s **Bloodthirsty Aerialist** and **Daybreak Charger** are tapped and can’t block flyers.\n\
\n\
3. **Card Advantage**:\n\
   - Attacking with three flyers will trigger **Tide Skimmer’s draw ability** and **Inniaz’s ability**, allowing us to steal one of their permanents.\n\
\n\
4. **Mana Efficiency**:\n\
   - We have 2 untapped Islands and can play another to reach {3}{U}{U} for Inniaz (reduced to {2}{U}{U}).\n\
   - Holding **Deem Worthy** and **Reptilian Reflection** for removal or cycling later.\n\
\n\
