  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Mulliganed a functional 7-card hand with 5 lands, a 3-drop creature, and premium removal. While land-heavy, the hand curves out with Prickly Marmoset on turn 3 and Deem Worthy on turn 5, and will naturally draw into more spells. Going to 6 risks a worse hand.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to mulligan to 6 cards",
      "better_line": "Keep the 7-card hand. While 5 lands is heavy, having a turn 3 play and strong removal spell is a functional start. Drawing into spells with guaranteed mana is better than risking a 6-card hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "MstMed Spike",
      "decision_index": 1,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Mulliganing a 7-card hand with 3 lands (2 Plains + Thriving Moor) and powerful late-game cards (Valorous Steed, Knight of the Tusk, Blessed Sanctuary). While the hand has no plays before turn 5 and Feast of Blood is likely dead, the mana base is solid and the top-end is excellent. Going to 6 risks getting a worse hand.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to mulligan to 6",
      "better_line": "Keep the 7-card hand. Three lands with powerful 5 and 6 drops is acceptable in Limited. Draw steps 1-4 give good chances to find early plays.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "G31FL Humble",
      "decision_index": 2,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With only 2 lands (both Swamps) in hand, Blood Price is a valuable card draw spell that could help find the additional lands and color sources desperately needed. Rodolf Duskbringer at 6 mana is too expensive to realistically cast soon with a 2-land hand, making it a better bottom candidate.",
      "action_taken": "Bottomed Blood Price, keeping Rodolf Duskbringer (6 mana) in a 2-land hand",
      "better_line": "Bottom Rodolf Duskbringer instead - it's the most expensive card and won't be castable for many turns with only 2 lands. Blood Price at 4 mana would help dig for the missing lands and White sources needed for Daybreak Charger and Valorous Steed.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 4,
      "player": "G31FL Humble",
      "decision_index": 4,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "The player passed priority in their postcombat main phase without playing a land, despite having three Islands in hand and one land drop remaining. This is turn 1, and playing a land is critical for developing mana to cast spells on subsequent turns. The player's hand contains Warden of Evos Isle (3 mana), Tide Skimmer (4 mana with Warden discount), and Inniaz (5 mana), all requiring early land drops to deploy on curve.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without playing a land, ending the turn with 0 lands on the battlefield.",
      "better_line": "Play an Island to have 1 mana available and be on track to curve out with Warden of Evos Isle on turn 3.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 10,
      "player": "MstMed Spike",
      "decision_index": 7,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Daybreak Charger in postcombat main wastes its ETB +2/+0 trigger (only target is itself, and combat is over). Waiting until next turn's precombat main would allow it to enter, target itself for +2/+0, and immediately attack as a 5/1 instead of a 3/1.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Daybreak Charger postcombat on turn 4, wasting the +2/+0 ETB",
      "better_line": "Hold Daybreak Charger until next turn's precombat main phase, cast it targeting itself for +2/+0, then attack as a 5/1 for 2 more damage",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 31,
      "player": "G31FL Humble",
      "decision_index": 15,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "MstMed Spike timed out and failed to cast any spell with 3 untapped Islands. Warden of Evos Isle (2/2 flyer for {2}{U}) was castable and would provide a flying blocker against the opponent's Bloodthirsty Aerialist, while also reducing future flying creature costs (making Tide Skimmer, Roaming Ghostlight, and Inniaz cheaper). At 12 life facing an opponent with creatures on board, developing the board is critical. Missing this play wastes an entire turn's mana and delays the game plan significantly.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and passed without casting anything.",
      "better_line": "Cast Warden of Evos Isle for {2}{U} to get a 2/2 flyer on board as a blocker and cost reducer for future flying creatures like Tide Skimmer and Inniaz.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 83,
      "player": "MstMed Spike",
      "decision_index": 29,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Spike is stuck on 3 lands with a hand full of 4-5 mana spells (Inniaz, Roaming Ghostlight, Tide Skimmer, Rooting Moloch all cost 4-5 mana). At 12 life facing Bloodthirsty Aerialist and Daybreak Charger, they desperately need to find lands to start deploying threats. Cycling Rooting Moloch for {2} would dig toward a land drop while Spike is mana-screwed.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without cycling Rooting Moloch",
      "better_line": "Cycle Rooting Moloch for {2} to dig for a 4th land. Finding land enables Warden of Evos Isle next turn (which then makes the 5-mana flyers cheaper). Staying on 3 lands means continuing to do nothing while the opponent builds their board and pressures Spike's 12 life total.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 90,
      "player": "MstMed Spike",
      "decision_index": 31,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarded Rooting Moloch, which has Cycling {2} (payable with just Islands), over Reptilian Reflection, which requires both red mana to be on the battlefield AND cycling cards to function. With only Islands in play and no red sources, Rooting Moloch's generic cycling cost made it the most usable of the red cards as a way to dig for lands.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Rooting Moloch",
      "better_line": "Discard Reptilian Reflection, which requires both red mana and cycling synergy to function, keeping Rooting Moloch's cheap cycling ability as a way to dig for land drops and red sources.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 107,
      "player": "MstMed Spike",
      "decision_index": 38,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 7 life facing 5 damage (2/3 flying Bloodthirsty Aerialist + 3/1 Daybreak Charger), declining to cast Unsubstantiate on the Aerialist drops Spike to 2 life instead of 4 life. At 2 life, Spike dies to virtually any attack next turn. Bouncing the Aerialist also removes the most dangerous threat (flying creature that grows with life gain) and forces opponent to spend 3 mana recasting it.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, taking the full 5 damage and going to 2 life.",
      "better_line": "Cast Unsubstantiate targeting Bloodthirsty Aerialist to bounce it, taking only 3 damage (going to 4 life) and forcing opponent to recast the growing flyer. This buys crucial time and survival margin while Spike develops their board with Warden of Evos Isle and flying creatures.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 113,
      "player": "MstMed Spike",
      "decision_index": 41,
    }
  ],
